Feature: Setting up the TX15
  There are two parts: the radio, and the sim.

  In the radio, put the radio in USB joystick mode: plug it in with the USB cable, and choose
  USB Joystick (HID) when EdgeTX asks. The sim sees every channel of the radio as an axis. A
  switch is a channel too, so the arm and mode switches need no special setting if your model sends them: they are
  channels that go from low, through the middle, to high. If your model does not send
  a switch, add a channel for it in the mixer, after the channels of the sticks. Set the model up
  as a plain plane with the channel order aileron, elevator, throttle and rudder, and no
  mixing, because the autopilot does the mixing.

  In the sim, press F2, and do the steps on the screen. The sim asks for the sticks first. Then
  it asks for the switches, one at a time, and you flip the one you want. Each one is optional,
  and Enter skips it. These are our suggestions for the TX15:

  Channel 5 is ARDUPILOT ARM, on SE. When SE is pressed in, the autopilot arms the plane; out,
  it disarms the plane. Channel 8 is ARDUPILOT MODE, a mix of SA and SB. The sim sends it to
  the autopilot as it is, and the autopilot divides it into six positions. Each position is a
  flight mode. The six modes, from the lowest position to the highest, are QHOVER, QLOITER,
  FBWA, CRUISE, AUTO and QRTL. In the mixer, give channel 8 the weight 52% of SB plus 13% of
  SA, with an offset of -2%: SA down and SB down, middle and up give the first three modes,
  and SA up gives the last three.

  The keys of the keyboard and the buttons of a gamepad work too: they step through the six
  modes one at a time, and they change the arm signal one press at a time. The other three
  functions, LAUNCH, RESET and CAMERA, matter only when you fly the plain T1-S from the radio.
  Give them buttons of your choice, or skip them.

  Expectation: F2 calibrates the radio
    The calibration needs the radio. If you do not have a radio, the sim tells you to connect
    one. The sim saves the calibration when it ends, and you can do it again at any time.
    Given the radio is not calibrated
    When the pilot calibrates the radio
    Then the radio is calibrated
